From b8bd9e731f92c8b0ec4eab87ae29cb828613f9f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: elkir0 <elkir0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/16] misc: mipi-lli: port the Exynos5433 MIPI-LLI driver for
 the SS333 modem

Port Samsung's MIPI-LLI controller and M-PHY driver (kernel_universal5433
drivers/misc/mipi-lli/, include/linux/mipi-lli.h, GPLv2) to 6.12 as one
module, exynos5433-mipi-lli.ko (CONFIG_MIPI_LLI), for the link between the
Exynos5433 and the Shannon SS333 modem of the SM-T715.  The 3.10 file
names are kept so that diff -ru against that tree stays the review tool.
Design: research/modem/research/analysis/kernel_port_design.md 2.1-2.8,
SYNTHESIS.md D1-D3, kernel_boot_review.md 3 and 5.1-5.3.

API: include/linux/mipi-lli.h keeps the 3.10 prototypes modem_v1 uses and
the link states (LLI_UNMOUNTED 0, LLI_MOUNTED 1, LLI_WAITFORMOUNT 2).
Every call is safe before the driver is bound; mipi_lli_get_phys_base()
and _size() return 0 until then.  mipi_lli_get_pm_svc() is gone (no link
PM FSM in phase 1).  New: mipi_lli_hw_allowed(), mipi_lli_remap_ok() and
mipi_lli_wait_reset_done().

allow_hw module parameter (default 0, root-writable): with 0 the probe
maps the four register ranges (lli, remote, sysreg, mphy), looks up the
PMU syscon, the memory-region, the clocks and the IRQs, requests both IRQs
with IRQF_NO_AUTOEN, and touches no clock gate and no LLI, M-PHY or PMU
register; every explicit action returns -EPERM or does nothing.  With 1,
hw_init (debugfs, or the first mipi_lli_reset/intr_enable) enables the
clocks once, writes LLI_PHY_CON = 1 through the PMU regmap, masks and
clears the LLI interrupts and enables the IRQs.  The driver core still
applies the node's assigned-clocks before probe (CMU only, as 3.10 did).

Interlocks:
 - the probe binds only on memory-region 0xde000000 + 8 MiB (anything
   else needs shmem_unsafe_base=1), power-of-two size, size-aligned base,
   no System RAM in the region (a failed reservation still prints its
   "OF: reserved mem" line) nor in the 256 MiB CP window above its base;
 - IAL_LL/BE_INIT_ADDR_REMAP is programmed at each SW_RESET_DONE (0x0001BC97
   for the board region, checked by static_assert and a probe self-test);
   the remap registers and LLI_PHY_CON are read back there and set
   remap_ok, which every reset clears;
 - HIBERN8_EXIT_DONE writes LLI_MOUNT_CTRL only while remap_ok, else logs
   "lli: mount refused (remap %08x/%08x)";
 - RESET_ON_ERROR_SENT is cleared (W1C) before its soft reset, which is
   limited to roe_reset_limit per second; more than irq_storm_limit (1000)
   link or sig_irq_storm_limit (10000) signal interrupts per second
   disable the IRQ until the next reset;
 - the M-PHY AFC branch runs until a mount with DL credits has saved the
   AFC code (phy->afc_valid), instead of only in the first cmn_init after
   boot, so a reset without a mount no longer forces AFC code 0.

Kept from 3.10: the controller settings and the three M-PHY tuning
tables (the Exynos5433 + SS333 branch made unconditional), the hard/
threaded IRQ logic, the re-arm on UNMOUNT_DONE, the "lli: " message
texts, lli_control's "MIPI-LLI %x\n" show format.  lli_control's store
accepts only 0 (debug dump), and 1-3 only with lli_debug_cmds=1 and
allow_hw=1.  debugfs mipi-lli/status (software state; registers only
with the clocks on), mipi-lli/hw_init and mipi-lli/reset (hw_init +
intr_enable + soft reset: gate G3, CP held in reset).

Dropped: the link PM callbacks, the loopback test, the register dump
work and its 5430 clock table, store commands 4-6/98/99, the shared
memory vmap, system and runtime PM callbacks, every panic and BUG, the
remove callback and module_exit (suppress_bind_attrs); no
MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE, so the module is never autoloaded from the DT.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
